Provenance (recorded by AnvilMac, 2026-11-10):
  Local fix for DXMT main 647b0020ba5764e5593b12407afd76964fa11e20, after patches 0001 and 0004-0007.
  Local changes: LGPL-2.1-or-later (DXMT after v0.80 is LGPL-2.1-or-later; see upstream COPYING.LIB).
  Local implementation Copyright 2026 Mahdi Taziki.
  Upstream commit 914ae9a28ef2 ("feat(airconv): implement gs with dynamic index buffer view", 2026-10-26) changed
  `if (index_buffer_idx != ~0u)` to `else if (index_buffer_idx)`. A draw without an index buffer leaves
  index_buffer_idx at ~0u, which is true, so the vertex stage before a geometry shader took the indexed path
  (function->getArg(~0u)) and failed to convert: "Failed to compile shader:" then "Failed to create mesh PSO:
  Invalid vertex shader.". Seen in Void's Cave (Unreal Engine 5 demo, black 3D scene) and in an original no-window
  D3D11 probe (one triangle through a pass-through geometry shader, DXMT's shader cache off): Draw stayed black and
  DrawIndexed drew; with this patch both draw, and Void's Cave draws at 60 fps without errors (owner, 2026-11-10).
  Still unfixed on DXMT main 6e69d0f (2026-11-04).
diff --git a/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp b/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
index 62cd031..d97798d 100644
--- a/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
+++ b/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
@@ -793,7 +793,7 @@ convert_dxbc_vertex_for_geometry_shader(
       builder.CreateBr(finalize_index);
     }
 
-  } else if (index_buffer_idx) {
+  } else if (index_buffer_idx != ~0u) {
     auto start_index = builder.CreateExtractValue(draw_arguments, 2);
     auto index_buffer = function->getArg(index_buffer_idx);
     auto index_buffer_element_type = index_buffer->getType()->getNonOpaquePointerElementType();
